        <body>
            <div xml:id="d230">

                <pb facs="0423" n="361" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg361"/>

                <head>No. 225.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Read
                        to Mr. Evarts</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Athens</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-01-26"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 26, 1878</date>.
                        (Received February 16.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 343.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my No. 338, I have the honor
                    to report that the Greek Chamber passed yesterday a bill by which the
                    importation duties upon cotton seed and cleansed or uncleansed cotton are
                    abolished.</p>
                <p>The above bill will take effect from the day of its ratification by the King and
                    publication.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN MEREDITH REA</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
